## Planned regressions

Planned regression: output-only seat cwd cannot resolve a marker that exists
only in the checkout, while its prompt input remains readable.

Planned regression: opted-in live-run seat cwd resolves the checkout marker and
the resulting GateAttempt records read_checkout true.

Planned regression: opted-in supervised gate materializes the captured stage SHA
for the seat while deterministic checks still execute in the caller worktree.

Planned regression: every seat receives a byte-identical prompt containing the
authoritative-provenance, no-rederived-arithmetic, falsification-only, and
block-with-evidence instructions.

Planned regression: false/absent access prompts explicitly say output-only and
the gate record omits read_checkout.

Each filesystem-absence test contains a positive control: the same recorder or
runner reads the marker when given the granted checkout, proving that an empty
observation is not caused by broken instrumentation.

