KNOWN LIMITATION (disclosed, tracked): GitHub issue #14 is still open. Until it
lands, `worktree.Checkout` does not populate submodules or record their SHAs, so
this child proves only ordinary non-submodule repositories. The implementation
must not claim submodule coverage. If #14 lands before final review, rebase,
integrate its manifest shape, and add the submodule regression. Otherwise the PR
body must say the submodule path is untested and depends on #14. Reviewers should
judge whether that is acceptable scope for this PR-only deliverable or a blocker.

## L2 author declarations

TOPOLOGY: one gate orchestrator invokes seats sequentially today. The change
adds no concurrent writer. Each output-only seat gets a distinct neutral cwd;
granted seats share the already-existing read-only-by-contract pinned checkout.

DURABILITY CLASS: no irreversible operation. Gate attempts retain the existing
at-most-once CAS append per round; the new boolean is part of that same manifest
write. Temp checkout/cwd creation is reversible and cleaned up.

COMPLETE SET / all-sites enumeration: every seat-execution site is the single
`runGateSeats` helper; its two callers are `GateStage` and `runGate`. Every gate
record construction site is those same two callers. Every seat-prompt path is
enumerated above and must receive the rule. No other model-seat invocation is in
the liverun package.

TRUST BOUNDARY: workflow YAML and captured run manifests are untrusted until
their existing strict decoders validate them. The resolved boolean, captured
stage `git_sha`, and checkout returned by `worktree.Checkout` are trusted facts
rooted in those validators plus git object resolution. Stage output and model
seat behavior are untrusted. Arbitrary same-process code execution is outside
scope; configured external seat commands are trusted to obey their registry
read-only/no-tools modes and the prompt's no-edit rule.

IRREVERSIBLE SEQUENCES: none

